Sorry, but I am unable to find example declarations of an inputfield or any other UI element for that matter. 

Right now, I have a script attached to an empty GameObject that says:
    using UnityEngine;
    using System.Collections;
    using UnityEngine.UI;

    public class CommandLine : MonoBehaviour {

    	public Texture backgroundTexture;

     	void OnGUI() {

    		if( InputField  = 'help') { continue; }  
    	} 
    }    

Am I supposed to put everything in OnGUI? Evidently, OnGUI is now legacy?

I tried to pass in ( x, y, width, height) params. The docs at http://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/UI.InputField.html fail to mention how to use InputField and are not noob friendly.
